# WarnFlux: bring up the packet link on the modem's DATA interface.
#
# This script runs on /dev/serial/by-id/usb-HUAWEI_Technology_HUAWEI_Mobile-if04-port0
# (the E173's modem/data interface). The station's SMS session keeps the AT/PCUI
# interface (if00, mapped into the container as /dev/modem), so dialling here
# never locks the panel out of the SIM.
ABORT BUSY
ABORT 'NO CARRIER'
ABORT 'NO DIALTONE'
ABORT ERROR
ABORT 'NO ANSWER'
TIMEOUT 30

# The data interface DOES answer AT (the silent port is if03, see README).
# A failed dial for now: on 2026-11-06 the operator refused every data call
# (NO CARRIER) although the PDP context activates — the SIM has no data
# service. -s keeps that visible in the journal instead of being swallowed.
#
# Once the operator enables data, this script is the sequence that worked on
# the bench: attach the packet domain by hand (the modem does not do it alone),
# then dial. The station's SMS session is on if00 and is not affected.
'' AT
OK ATE0
OK AT+CGATT=1
OK ATD*99***1#
CONNECT ''
